\noindent
The $8\times8$ win in full, from the diagram on the previous page: seventeen
moves, Black to play, six plies to a board. Each board is where the one before
it left off, White's moves are green and Black's red, and the arrows are
numbered in playing order. The value falls by exactly one at every ply ---
$+33, -32, +31, \ldots, +1$ --- which is the certificate that neither side has
anything better.

